{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Because Abraham listened to My voice.</b> In all that I commanded him." "<b>And kept My charge.</b> He continually performed the charge specially devoted to Me — that is, to bestow kindness, as it says: כָּל אָרְחוֹת ה' חֶסֶד וֶאֱמֶת (Psalms 25:10), and to guide sinners on the way. This he did when he called in the name of YHWH, and he also kept <b>My commandments, My statutes, and My teachings</b> that the sons of Noah were commanded; and so he was worthy both to seek and to fulfill, as an exemplar to the many. See: to Isaac He now attributed merit to others, and likewise below, in saying <b>and I will multiply your seed for the sake of Abraham My servant</b> — but so He did not say to Jacob, much less to Abraham. And this was before Isaac stirred himself to call in the name of YHWH; but after he called in the name of YHWH it is said <b>and Abimelech went to him from Gerar</b>, and they said <b>we have certainly seen that YHWH is with you; you are now blessed of YHWH</b>. And they no longer found him subject to the vexations of the jealous and disputes as at first. But to Jacob He did not attribute the merit of others at all, for he from his youth sat in tents to learn and to teach knowledge to the people — especially in the tents of Shem and Eber, where every seeker of YHWH gathered without doubt."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:49.367850390Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}